"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI patchset 1 exposed a Python-version-specific complexity-baseline failure: Python 3.13 reported src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py::_dispatch as stale while the worktree's Python 3.12 still measured it at C901 34. Remediated without changing behavior by partitioning the router along existing command-family seams and removing the now-obsolete _dispatch ceiling. Continuity remains explicit: legacy reconcile, jira-onboard, bridge-probe, bridge-fsck, and doctor routing/initialization policies are unchanged. Focused bridge + complexity + CLI-reference suite: 103 passed. make lint: PASS (active=69 new=0 increased=0 stale=0). make typecheck: PASS. Before the next Gerrit push I will re-fetch origin and update from origin/main, per operator instruction.","timestamp":1786146482074373001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 cleared the prior py3.13 complexity-baseline failure. Its py3.11 matrix then lost xdist worker gw3 while running unrelated tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted at 99%; 11,362 tests had passed, no assertion/traceback was emitted, the worker returned no coverage data, and this change touches no opcert code. Classified as a CI worker crash rather than a product finding and posted Gerrit `recheck`; retry run 31229199537 queued. LLM-Review remains +1 with zero unresolved comments.","timestamp":1786147649144218001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1527 / origin/main 45ad7d3ece after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. Retry CI run 31229199537 passed all Python lanes including the unrelated prior worker-loss lane. Focused 103 tests, lint, and typecheck passed before push; full CI passed after push. Marking the acceptance criteria complete from that evidence.","timestamp":1786148897443261001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Verification evidence for the gate criterion: source commit origin/main 45ad7d3ecea5791b45d144ac77d80d2d97068ef1; Gerrit change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1527 shows LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments; GitHub Actions retry https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31229199537 completed success across the full matrix. Local pre-push measurement in the repo venv: focused bridge/legacy suite 103 passed; make lint passed; make typecheck passed. The full make-test-equivalent default and integration suites passed in the cited CI run on Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13.","timestamp":1786149170001497001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier evidence map at merged ref 43448cd486:\n- Discovery/unknown-verb contracts: tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:35-66; parser exposes only preview/sync in src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:43-65.\n- Preview read-only and sync persisted mutation with unrelated-byte preservation: tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:95-138.\n- Rejected --mode, --filter-local-ids, and trailing args on both verbs: tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:69-92.\n- Help denylist and numeric-exit-code exclusion: tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:151-165.\n- Five legacy Mode values/caps and real reconcile-check ref round trip: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py:37-117 and tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py:144-158.\n- Legacy reconcile default: tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py:168-176. Doctor, jira-onboard, bridge-probe, and bridge-fsck remain on their existing dispatch paths and suites named in the criterion.\n- Nested CLI-reference generation: tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py::test_render_expands_the_staged_bridge_group; staged docs are docs/cli-reference.md, docs/exit-codes.md, docs/user-guide.md, and docs/release-notes.md.\nExternal gate evidence remains in the existing [operator-attested] comment: Gerrit 1527 and successful full CI run 31229199537.","timestamp":1786156559773164001}],"created_at":1786142317990206001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"870d716f-1a19-48d6-bba2-6fb0161878e1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8145-0930-10f4-459f"},{"link_uuid":"5b5ff197-11f2-4b65-b262-ae2e187f3a61","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0e53-8421-5190-45b7"}],"description":"## Context\n\nEstablish the nested `rebar bridge` CLI through a shippable vertical slice. The parent story originally proposed advertising all eight final verbs before their owning stories implemented them. That would expose broken placeholders on `main`. This task therefore registers only the two verbs it owns now: `preview` and `sync`. Later dependency-ordered stories extend the group only when each handler is functional.\n\n`preview` is the read-only path over the existing reconciler dry-run mode. `sync` is the mutating path over the existing live mode. The legacy top-level `reconcile`, `jira-onboard`, `bridge-probe`, and `bridge-fsck` spellings remain unchanged at this boundary.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py` as the nested-group parser and shared reconciler subprocess launcher.\n- Keep `_cli._reconcile` as a compatibility wrapper around that launcher until story `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51` retires the top-level verb.\n- Route the help-backed `bridge` noun from `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py`.\n- Register only `preview` and `sync`: preview forces `dry-run`; sync forces `live`.\n- Reject `--mode`, `--filter-local-ids`, and arbitrary trailing arguments so callers cannot override the read/write distinction. The public `--max-changes`, `--only`, `--except`, and `--max-age` flags do not exist yet; story `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51` will add them together with their behavior and migration.\n- Define exact discovery contracts: no nested verb prints group usage; `--help` prints usage; an unknown nested verb fails with the valid choices and never falls through to a same-named top-level command.\n- Update `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` and regenerate `docs/cli-reference.md` for the nested group; add the new dispatcher arms and exit contracts to `docs/exit-codes.md`; update `docs/user-guide.md` with preview-versus-sync guidance; and update `docs/release-notes.md` to announce only the staged surface that actually ships.\n- Keep public help free of the parent story's exact internal-vocabulary denylist: `mode`, `rank`, `gate`, `lock`, `cap`, `pass`, `binding store`, and numeric exit-code values.\n- Preserve `Mode`, `MODE_CAPS`, the `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"` round trip, top-level `doctor`, and all legacy bridge spellings.\n\n## Surface parity\n\n- CLI: in scope and exercised through the real `rebar` entrypoint.\n- Library and MCP: out of scope; story `f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d` owns those surfaces.\n- Automated workflows and scripts: out of scope; story `4a44-4abb-ae91-4e51` owns their migration.\n- Dual direction: both preview/read and sync/write are proven here.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse a real CLI subprocess against a temporary git-backed tracker plus a stateful fake Jira transport built from production-shaped fixtures. A unit-only dispatch test is insufficient because parsing, subprocess wiring, mode selection, and persisted state are contractual.\n\nRED-first oracle:\n- happy path: `rebar bridge preview` returns the real reconciler JSON plan;\n- held out: exact before/after snapshots prove preview performs zero Jira writes and zero ticket or bridge-state writes;\n- held out: sync starts from an unbound remote-only issue, creates the real local/binding mutation, and preserves unrelated event bytes;\n- held out: no-verb, help, unknown verb, top-level-name collision, forbidden flag, phase-gate, doctor, legacy-command, generated-reference, and exit-code-table contracts; the help oracle lowercases captured output and rejects every literal denylisted term and any numeric exit-code value;\n- mutation: routing preview to live must fail the no-write oracle; routing sync to dry-run must fail the persisted-mutation oracle.\n\nThis wrapper adds no new composed store operation, retry loop, or cache, so the shared contention suites remain the responsibility of the reconciler core.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge`, `rebar bridge --help`, `rebar bridge preview --help`, and `rebar bridge sync --help` expose only functional `preview` and `sync` verbs with pinned exit/stream contracts.\n- [x] An unknown nested verb fails with valid choices and never dispatches a same-named top-level command.\n- [x] `bridge preview` performs zero Jira writes and zero ticket or bridge-state writes, proven by exact snapshots and the fake transport log.\n- [x] `bridge sync` performs a persisted mutation from a production-shaped fake Jira fixture while preserving unrelated state.\n- [x] `--mode`, `--filter-local-ids`, and unknown arguments are rejected on both verbs.\n- [x] Captured `bridge`, `preview`, and `sync` help contains none of `mode`, `rank`, `gate`, `lock`, `cap`, `pass`, `binding store`, or numeric exit-code values.\n- [x] `Mode`, `MODE_CAPS`, and `gated_mode: \"reconcile-check\"` remain intact and exercised by `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py`.\n- [x] Top-level `doctor`, `reconcile`, `jira-onboard`, `bridge-probe`, and `bridge-fsck` behavior remains unchanged; continuity is exercised by `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py::test_legacy_reconcile_keeps_dry_run_default` plus the existing `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py`, `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py`, and `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py` suites.\n- [x] `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` generates the nested group, proven by `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py::test_render_expands_the_staged_bridge_group`; `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, and `docs/release-notes.md` describe only the staged surface that ships.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Focused pytest nodes, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` pass.\n\n## Rollback\n\nThis is additive and changes no persisted schema. Revert the single Gerrit change to remove the nested group while leaving every legacy spelling intact.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"new nested bridge parser and shared reconciler launcher"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"route the bridge noun and retain the legacy reconcile compatibility wrapper"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt","reason":"help-backed group, preview, and sync usage contract"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt","reason":"advertise the new bridge noun"},{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"generate the nested group without advertising unimplemented verbs"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli.py","reason":"real CLI subprocess oracle for preview/sync state and error contracts"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"register the new help-backed noun in the overview contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"pin generated nested-group reference coverage"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document preview versus sync and staged verb attachment"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated CLI reference for the nested group"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"document new bridge dispatcher arms and nonzero contracts"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"announce the additive staged bridge surface without claiming legacy retirement"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1786441293771687001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","4752-3afb-e8bd-448a"],["relates_to","0e53-8421-5190-45b7"],["relates_to","8145-0930-10f4-459f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"4752-3afb-e8bd-448a","parent_status_uuid":"bf0f9edc-5144-45fd-928f-325a189b2cb4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bridge","cli","ux"],"ticket_id":"b42a-ffc3-deeb-4491","ticket_type":"task","title":"Add safe bridge noun with functional preview and sync","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["61a8ad4b-44a9-42bf-a86e-a561d24e4cbc","ff67c06f-740c-498f-b97a-7333b270b96c","448bfe34-d1d2-4ef2-95c3-08d3522abe97","88441dda-a506-4d31-ac09-a52b74635f7e","df089767-612e-4d5e-bce6-fd7b6df379e6","5a528574-5df3-4d06-88c6-5dcc8439f52f","0ca50d36-ba89-4636-ae6f-6e2ddd643239","8bc749ca-8cc5-4e33-aac1-dc8926941e68","2e3d2c91-e09a-4855-b2bb-07bd5cef9486","bf0f9edc-5144-45fd-928f-325a189b2cb4","84787695-d8a3-47a0-a181-acf5c1174037"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659653364588001,"uuid":"6064af09-3b6e-4248-8273-bf2ba7cd24c1"}